{"id":"NCT07644559","title":"A Phase 2 Study of VS-7375 in Patients With KRAS G12D-Mutated Pancreatic Cancer","official":"A Phase 2, Open-label Study of VS-7375, an Oral KRAS G12D (ON/OFF) Inhibitor, as Monotherapy and With Cetuximab, in Patients With Metastatic KRAS G12D-Mutated Pancreatic Cancer (TARGET-D 201)","summary":"This study will assess the safety and efficacy of VS-7375 alone and in combination with cetuximab in patients with metastatic KRAS G12D - mutated Pancreatic Cancer","conditions":["Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma (PDAC)","G12D Mutated KRAS"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"VS-7375"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"cetuximab (or panitumumab if α-gal IgE+ or cetuximab reaction)"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Histologic or cytologic confirmed PDAC\n* Measurable disease per RECIST 1.1\n* Local testing confirmed KRAS G12D mutation (tissue required for confirmatory central testing)\n* ECOG PS=0 or 1\n\nAdequate organ function\n\nVS-7375 + cetuximab (2L PDAC) :\n\n-Received only 1 prior Tx in the metastatic setting; prior adjuvant counts as a line if progressed within 6 months\n\nVS-7375 + cetuximab (1L PDAC) :\n\n-Treatment-naïve or received ≤ 1 cycle of SoC for metastatic disease\n\nExclusion criteria:\n\n* Have any documented co-existing pathogenic or likely pathogenic RAS mutation(s) in KRAS\n* Prior anti-cancer Tx within 4 weeks or drug-specific timeline within first treatment dose, whichever shorter\n* Major surgery within 4 weeks of first treatment dose\n* Radiation therapy (RT) within 1 week of first treatment dose; RT to brain or lung within 2 weeks of first treatment dose\n* History of drug-induced Interstitial Lung Disease\n* Receipt of prior direct RAS inhibitor\n* Untreated or symptomatic CNS metastasis\n* Receipt of strong CYP3A4 inhibitor/inducer or CYP3A4 sensitive substrates with narrow therapeutic index within 14 days or drug-specific timeline within first treatment dose, whichever is shorter\n* Receipt of PPI, P-CABs, or H2 blocker within 5 days\n* Inability to swallow oral medication\n* Other protocol-defined inclusion/exclusion criteria may apply","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":185,"start":"2026-06-16","pcd":"2027-06","upd":"2026-11-06","sponsor":"Verastem, Inc.","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Verastem Call Center · 7812924204 · VS-7375-201TrialSupport@verastem.com","Luke Chung, MD · VS-7375-201Medical@verastem.com"],"sites":[{"f":"START- Los Angeles","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90025","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Hope Team · hopeteam@startresearch.com"},{"f":"Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90048","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Zachariah Brown · 310-423-5618 · Zachariah.Brown@cshs.org"},{"f":"Valkyrie Clinical Trials","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90067","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Trenis Palmer · 4245351874 · trenis.palmer@vctcare.com"},{"f":"BRCR Global- Coral Springs","city":"Coral Springs","pr":"Florida","zip":"33065","s":"R","lat":26.2712,"lon":-80.2706,"c":"Sumit Sawhney · (561)447-0614 · ssawhney.md@brcrglobal.com"},{"f":"Mayo Clinical Florida","city":"Jacksonville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32224","s":"R","lat":30.3322,"lon":-81.6556,"c":"Clinical Trials Referral Office · 855-776-0015"},{"f":"BRCR Global- Tamarac","city":"Tamarac","pr":"Florida","zip":"33321","s":"R","lat":26.2129,"lon":-80.2498,"c":"Diana Casas · (561) 4470614 · dianac@brcrglobal.com"},{"f":"Moffitt Cancer Center","city":"Tampa","pr":"Florida","zip":"33612","s":"R","lat":27.9475,"lon":-82.4584,"c":"Brianna Holder · Brianna.Holder@moffitt.org"},{"f":"University of Chicago","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60637","s":"R","lat":41.85,"lon":-87.65,"c":"Cancer Clinical Trials Mailbox · cancerclinicaltrials@bsd.uchicago.edu"},{"f":"Johns Hopkins University","city":"Baltimore","pr":"Maryland","zip":"2128